/* Only applied when the checked-out Zephyr's devicetree actually defines
 * the hfclkaudio node label (see the detection in ../sysbuild.cmake).
 *
 * That node - and the clock_control_nrf_hfclkaudio driver that reads it -
 * arrived in Zephyr shortly after v4.4.2, which this project pins for CI.
 * A pinned v4.4.2 checkout has no such label, and referencing it there is a
 * devicetree parse error, not just a no-op - so it cannot live in the main
 * overlay unconditionally. But on a newer Zephyr the split clock_control_nrf
 * drivers select CLOCK_CONTROL_NRF_HFCLKAUDIO, which reads this node's
 * hfclkaudio-frequency property instead of the legacy &clock property the
 * main overlay sets, so without this fragment I2S's ACLK clock source
 * BUILD_ASSERT fails there.
 */
&hfclkaudio {
  hfclkaudio-frequency = <12288000>;
};
